<title>FRANCE: Rhone aids drug in phase two trials.</title>
<headline>Rhone aids drug in phase two trials.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pasteur Merieux Connaught, a unit of Rhone-Poulenc SA, said on Wednesday that one of its potential anti-aids drugs had started phase two clinical trials in the United States.</p>
<p>The trials will be conducted with Chron Vaccines and the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases.  </p>
<p>The tests will evaluate ALVAC-HIV vCP 205 of Pasteur Merieux and SF-2 rgp with MF59 of Chiron. The tests involve 420 adult volunteers.</p>
</text>
